1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,000
You bought Cribl to save money.
Can you show it?

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Every minute, Meter Reader
reads every flow through Cribl.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,500
It prices each one at what
its destination charges.

4
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:19,000
Where the pipeline cuts bytes,
it cuts dollars: $18,524 a day.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:23,000
You would have paid $1,503,380.
You paid $958,406.

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Saved by Cribl: $544,974.

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:33,000
An admin ships a pipeline change.
Meter Reader sees the commit.

8
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Meter Reader never changes a pipeline,
route, source or destination.

9
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:43,000
It watches the savings
ratio, minute by minute.

10
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Savings dropped 25 points
on this pipeline.

11
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Commit 22d0a5e, deployed by Steve Koelpin.

12
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:55,000
$1,250 a day. $456,250 a year.
Caught in 2:51.

13
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:01,000
In Slack, with a name on it.

14
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Restore the change. The savings come back.

15
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,000
The incident closes itself.

16
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:17,000
A weekly receipt goes to leadership.
They never open Cribl.

17
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Meter Reader by Steve Koelpin.

18
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Join the Cribl Innovators Network.
